- timestamp: '2026-11-08T09:30:25.528698+00:00'
  curator: Codex worker05 /root/buffer_tris
  action: WITHDRAW_UNSUPPORTED_COMPONENT_ID
  changes: Moore 1976 confirms the historical Clostridium leptum PY-maltose use; its
    referenced manual formulation remains unread. The current exact-strain DSM 753
    recipe has separate Trypticase peptone (BD BBL) and pepsin-digested meat peptone,
    5 g each, and a maltose modification. This comparator demonstrates why neither
    ingredient may be chosen for the historical single peptone edge without a source
    bridge. No comparator quantities are imported. Withdraw the unsupported peptone
    component_id and set reference_scope UNMAPPED; retain its existing component_name
    as historical interpretation, not a newly observed expanded source label. The
    original assertion method and UNKNOWN/PARTIAL completeness remain unchanged. This
    is a bounded part-reference correction only. Whole-owner identity, raw labels,
    occurrence counts, quantities, unrelated components, all historical evidence and
    source/role/export holds are preserved. Historical all-components-identified statements
    describe prior states, not a new approval. No new MappingEvidence is added; historical
    human/component evidence enums are not rewritten. Filed before this private correction
    at https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1176#issuecomment-6719248666.
  previous_status: MAPPED
  new_status: MAPPED
  llm_assisted: true
  llm_model: gpt-6
